# Fix: JWT Secret Validation Gap in Cross-Origin Deployments

## Context
Security review found that `validateEnv()` in `env.ts` only enforces SESSION_SECRET when `NODE_ENV === 'production'`, but `index.ts` treats cross-origin deployments as production too (`isProduction = NODE_ENV === 'production' || isCrossOrigin`). This means a cross-origin deployment without `NODE_ENV=production` starts with the publicly-known default JWT secret, enabling full auth bypass.

## Changes

### 1. `server/src/config/env.ts` — Align secret validation with cross-origin awareness

- Pass `CLIENT_URL` and `API_URL` through the same cross-origin check used in `index.ts`
- Reject the default secret when either `NODE_ENV === 'production'` OR the deployment is cross-origin
- This is the single critical fix

```ts
// In validateEnv():
const clientUrl = getEnvVarOrDefault('CLIENT_URL', 'http://localhost:5173');
const apiUrl = getEnvVarOrDefault('API_URL', 'http://localhost:3001');
const isCrossOrigin = new URL(clientUrl).origin !== new URL(apiUrl).origin;
const isEffectivelyProduction = isProduction || isCrossOrigin;

if (isEffectivelyProduction && sessionSecret === 'dev-secret-change-in-production') {
  throw new Error('SESSION_SECRET must be set to a secure value in production or cross-origin deployments');
}
```

### 2. `server/src/index.ts` — Exit on validation failure regardless of NODE_ENV

Currently lines 27-29 only `process.exit(1)` when `NODE_ENV === 'production'`. The validateEnv function already throws only when it should, so we should always exit on failure:

```ts
try {
  const envConfig = validateEnv();
  logEnvStatus(envConfig);
} catch (err) {
  console.error('Environment validation failed:', err);
  process.exit(1);
}
```

This is safe because `validateEnv()` only throws for the default secret in production/cross-origin — local dev with defaults won't throw.

## Files to Modify
- `server/src/config/env.ts` (lines 66-77)
- `server/src/index.ts` (lines 22-30)

## Verification
1. `npx tsc --noEmit` from `server/` — type check passes
2. Local dev still starts without SESSION_SECRET (same-origin localhost defaults)
3. Setting `CLIENT_URL=https://foo.vercel.app API_URL=https://bar.railway.app` without SESSION_SECRET should fail to start

