Perfect! Now I have a complete understanding of the bug. Let me create a summary document with all the findings:

## Summary

I've identified the **grandchild nesting bug** in the BeadsList (task list view) component. The issue is a **one-level-deep nesting limitation** caused by how the client filters and renders beads.

### Root Cause

**File:** `/Users/jason/playground/claudespace/dev-dash/client/src/components/beads/BeadsTree.tsx`

**Lines 164-212:** The `topLevelItems` computation builds a flat hierarchy with only one level of nesting:

```typescript
const topLevelItems = useMemo(() => {
  const childIds = new Set<string>();
  const parentIds = new Set<string>();
  const byId = new Map(deferredBeads.map((b) => [b.id, b]));

  // Identify parent-child relationships
  for (const bead of deferredBeads) {
    if (bead.parentBeadId && byId.has(bead.parentBeadId)) {
      childIds.add(bead.id);
      parentIds.add(bead.parentBeadId);
    }
  }

  // Group children by parent
  const childrenByParent = new Map<string, Bead[]>();
  for (const bead of deferredBeads) {
    if (bead.parentBeadId && parentIds.has(bead.parentBeadId)) {
      const list = childrenByParent.get(bead.parentBeadId) || [];
      list.push(bead);
      childrenByParent.set(bead.parentBeadId, list);
    }
  }

  // Build unified list: every bead that isn't a child becomes a top-level item
  const items: TopLevelItem[] = [];
  for (const bead of deferredBeads) {
    if (childIds.has(bead.id)) continue;  // <-- PROBLEM: filters out all non-top-level beads
    const isParent = parentIds.has(bead.id);
    const children = isParent ? topoSort(childrenByParent.get(bead.id) || []) : [];
    // ...
  }
}, [deferredBeads]);
```

### The Bug

1. **Line 191:** `if (childIds.has(bead.id)) continue;` — This **excludes ALL beads that have a parent**, regardless of depth.

2. **Lines 178-186:** Children are only grouped directly under their parent. Grandchildren (beads with `parentBeadId` pointing to a child) never appear in `childrenByParent` because:
   - A grandchild's parent is in `childIds` (it has its own parent)
   - The grandchild is never added to any parent's children array
   - The parent (child of root) only receives direct children

3. **Result:** When filtering by status (e.g., `in_progress`):
   - Parent 673949b7 appears (top-level)
   - Child 720c9e9d appears (has parent 673949b7)
   - 63 grandchildren of 720c9e9d are **invisible** because they're filtered out at line 191
   - The count is correct (63 in_progress) because counts are calculated on the full unfiltered dataset before nesting

### How Rendering Works

**Lines 389-476:** Only direct children are rendered:
```typescript
{isExpanded && (
  <div className="px-3 pb-3">
    <div className="ml-3 border-l border-theme-border">
      {item.children.map((child, idx) => {
        // Render child, but child.parentBeadId is never used to show grandchildren
      })}
    </div>
  </div>
)}
```

### Why the Count is Correct

**File:** `/Users/jason/playground/claudespace/dev-dash/client/src/components/beads/BeadsList.tsx`

**Line 202-218:** Filtering happens **after** fetching all beads from the server:
```typescript
const filteredBeads = beads.filter((bead) => {
  if (filter !== 'all' && bead.status !== filter) return false;
  // ... other filters
  return true;
});
```

Then **Line 747** passes `displayBeads` (the filtered list) to BeadsTree. But BeadsTree still only shows top-level and their direct children, so grandchildren remain hidden despite being in the filtered dataset.

### Additional Context

**File:** `/Users/jason/playground/claudespace/dev-dash/server/src/db/ops.ts`

**Lines 548-556:** The server correctly fetches all beads regardless of nesting depth. The `parentBeadId` parameter only filters if explicitly provided, which doesn't happen in the normal list view. The grandchildren exist in the dataset — they're just hidden by the client-side nesting logic.

### The Fix Needed

The BeadsTree component needs **recursive nesting** instead of single-level grouping:
- Build a hierarchical tree structure instead of a flat `parentBeadId → children` map
- Recursively render children that have other children
- Or expand the `TopLevelItem` interface to support unlimited nesting depth

